Edition No. 46 — Tuesday, 17 November 2026

9 stories: Friday for jurisdiction, Tuesday for liberty: the High Court rules on 20 November whether it can hear Mundubile and Zulu's sedition bail plea, and on 24 November on bail for the 18 (lead); The lawyers come in: LAZ says it will litigate if need be to keep the two-term limit, as a youth consortium sets a march on Parliament for 25 November and M'membe cries foul; 'Mapanza should not be left behind': Hichilema promises a dam on the Munyeke and Ng'onga rivers for wheat, says Zambia has never been better, and gives a school over K1 million; 'Not solely on how much revenue it generates': the UNDP asks the Treasury to shield poor households from the 2027 budget's taxes, as farmers decry the mobile money levy; A 54 per cent maize collapse and 23-hour blackouts, written into the books: the IMF credits Zambia with budgeting for climate risk and sets an October 2027 deadline; Ten held and four wanted over a hijacked copper truck: police say the Kafulafuta load was offloaded at a Twapia yard and the driver was promised US$200,000; A TikTok video from September, a charge under the Cyber Crimes Act in November: Ndola police arrest a 35-year-old woman over remarks about the President and release her on bond; 'Burundi managed to play when we had huge support, so why can't we play?': Zambia face Burundi at Stade Intwari at 15:00 today with second place in Group I to protect; Twenty-three tracks and half the industry: Rich Bizzy's 'Africa' gathers Chef 187, Macky 2, Chile One and JK, while Prince Luv and Yo Maps release 'Over'.


